      "node_id": "kg_doc_1",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Roger Donaldson (born 15 November 1945) is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer and writer whose films include \"The World's Fastest Indian\" (2005), acclaimed 1981 relationship drama \"Smash Palace\", and a run of titles shot in the United States, including the Kevin Costner films \"No Way Out\" (1987) and \"Thirteen Days\" (2000), and the 1997 disaster film \"Dante's Peak\".",
